{"name":"Plastic Cheese","hex":"#ffcc04","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plastic cheese","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any soft cheese that can be moulded.","Any processed cheese of an inferior quality, often sliced and wrapped in plastic film."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plastic_cheese"}],"entries":[{"title":"Processed cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Processed cheese is a product made from cheese mixed with an emulsifying agent. Additional ingredients, such as unfermented dairy ingredients, salt, vegetable oils, sugar, or food coloring may be included. As a result, many flavors, colors, and textures of processed cheese exist. Processed cheese typically contains around 50–60% cheese and 40–50% other ingredients."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Eru_goudkuipje_sambal.jpg/330px-Eru_goudkuipje_sambal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Processed_cheese","wikidata":"Q1570052"},{"title":"Plastic","blocks":[{"text":"Plastics are a wide range of synthetic or semisynthetic materials composed primarily of polymers. Their defining characteristic, plasticity, allows them to be molded, extruded, or pressed into a diverse range of solid forms. This adaptability, combined with a wide range of other properties such as low weight, durability, flexibility, chemical resistance, low toxicity, and low-cost production, has led to their widespread use around the world. While most plastics are produced from natural gas and petroleum, a growing minority are produced from renewable resources like polylactic acid."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Plastic_household_items.jpg/330px-Plastic_household_items.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plastic","wikidata":"Q11474"},{"title":"Cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Cheese is a type of dairy product produced in a range of flavors, textures, and forms by curdling of milk, usually from cows, goats or sheep, and sometimes of water buffalo. During production, milk is usually acidified and either the enzymes of rennet or bacterial enzymes with similar activity are added to cause the protein casein to coagulate. The solid curds, consisting of proteins and milkfat, are then separated from the liquid whey and pressed into finished cheese. Some cheeses have aromatic molds on the outer layer or rind, while others have them throughout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Cheese_platter.jpg/330px-Cheese_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheese","wikidata":"Q10943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Provel.jpg/500px-Provel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Provel.jpg/500px-Provel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 5-pound block of Provel \"pasteurized process cheddar, swiss, and provolone cheese\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProvel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Processed_cheese_1.jpg/500px-Processed_cheese_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Processed_cheese_1.jpg/1280px-Processed_cheese_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Processed_cheese_1.jpg/500px-Processed_cheese_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Slices of processed cheese","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProcessed_cheese_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wiki